            <div xml:id="d520-a1">

                <pb facs="0904" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg808"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 24]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Passport of the boy Hussein</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>[Revenue-stamp, 2 rubles.]</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">Commanderof Zarafshan District. Chancery. Div. of Adm August,
                        1873. Samarcand. No. 2790.</seg> Mr. Eugene Schuyler, of the American
                    legation at our imperial court during his stay in Bokhara ransomed a Persian
                    slave, a boy eight years old, by name <hi rendition="#italic">Hussein</hi>, whom
                    he has retained with him until he finds the possibility of returning him to his
                    native country.</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">Description: Eyes, black. Face, clean quiet.</seg> For
                    confirmation of this, this passport is given, with iriy signature and the
                    crown-seal</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">Nose, Mouth,} ordinary. Height, 1 ershin, 6 berslioks.</seg>
                    Commander of the Zarafshan district.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Major-General</hi>
                    ABRAMOFF.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">l.s.</hi>]</p>
                    <p>Director of Chancery, Artillery-Staff Captain, (name illegible.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
